BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Data\, Cloud and AI in Mexico City|Bob TV Episode 4: Why generic A
 I fails at mainframe scale - and what works|Online
DTSTART:20261201T100000
CATEGORIES:ai,cloud,data,web
DESCRIPTION:Data\, Cloud and AI in Mexico City\nJoin us for the fourth epi
 sode of Bob TV\, the monthly digital event series hosted by Max Jesch\, IB
 M Bob’s outbound product manager. Each month\, Max sits down with a tech
 nical guest to explore real examples of your trusted AI assistant in actio
 n—showing how Bob accelerates enterprise software development across the
  entire lifecycle.\nFeaturing Special Guest: Ethan Mendel\, Development Le
 ad\, IBM Z premium package for Bob\nEthan will discuss why mainframe moder
 nization is hard — and why AI alone is not enough.\n\n* The real scope o
 f the challenge: 10-year modernization timelines\, skill shortages\, and t
 echnical debt that runs so deep some clients haven't touched certain progr
 ams in decades\n* Why generic AI falls short: LLMs achieve only \\~30% acc
 uracy on non-trivial impact analysis questions for large mainframe applica
 tions — hallucination gets worse as scale increases\n* The Premium Packa
 ge for Z approach: static code analytics + metadata-enriched model intelli
 gence as the foundation\, not a replacement for AI but a way to make AI re
 liable at enterprise scale\n\nBob TV is your monthly window into Bob capab
 ilities:\n\n* AI assisted development workflows\n* Enterprise modernizatio
 n patterns\n* Agent based software engineering\n\n**Host:**\n**![](https:/
 /cache.webcasts.com/content/ibmx001/1771850/content/8605de84345dc42143086f
 23cfcb2d55984805ea/common/Screenshot20260803at1.28.53PM.png)Maximilian Jes
 ch**\, Outbound Product Manager\, IBM Bob\n\n![](https://cache.webcasts.co
 m/content/ibmx001/1781965/content/757422b7d448e30f3b8159a77a44b5cfcd8c0f05
 /common/EthanMendel1.png)**Ethan Mendel**\, Development Lead\, IBM Z premi
 um package for IBM Bob
LOCATION:Online event\,
END:VEVENT
