BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup|Dec 
 8 - How to Let Long-tail Guide Your 3D Annotation Workshop|Online
DTSTART:20261208T110000
CATEGORIES:ai,data,frontend,mobile
DESCRIPTION:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\
 nJoin us on Dec 8 for the “How to Let Long-tail Guide Your 3D Annotation
 ” workshop with [Eric Hofesmann](https://www.linkedin.com/in/eric-hofesm
 ann/).\n\n**Date\, Time and Location**\n\nDec 08\, 2026\n9:00 AM - 10:00 A
 M PST\nOnline. **[Register for the Zoom!](https://voxel51.com/events/how-t
 o-let-long-tail-guide-your-3d-annotation-december-8-2026)**\n\nAutonomous 
 driving models rarely fail on the common case. They fail on the long-tail:
  the pedestrian stepping out from behind a parked truck or a construction 
 zone that matches nothing in the training set. Each of those moments lives
  in synchronized multi-sensor data\, made up of a LiDAR sweep\, a ring of 
 cameras\, a timestamp\, and a calibration. Fixing one means finding it\, l
 abeling it in 3D\, and proving the next model handles it.\n\nIn this live 
 session\, we will take long-tail driving scenarios from discovery to 3D la
 bels to evaluation\, and make the case that 3D ground truth should be buil
 t where your data lives\, not exported away from it.
LOCATION:Online event\,
END:VEVENT
